<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cumberland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cumberland is a historic county in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solway-firth">Solway Firth</a> and the Lake District, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlisle">Carlisle</a> as its chief town. Once part of the British kingdom of Strathclyde, it was disputed between Scottish and English kings: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> held it during the English civil war of Stephen and Matilda, until Henry II recovered it in 1157.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cumberland.jpg" alt="Cumberland" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Walsh · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skiddaw_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
